11. Technical Specification: Physis‑α Reference Workcell

The Physis‑α workcell embodies the architecture in hardware. Two Franka Research 3 arms with joint torque sensing and impedance control at 1 kHz, an ISO 9409‑1 quick‑change system supporting gripper, FDM print head, laser profilometer, and vacuum tool. Four Intel RealSense D435i cameras, a FLIR A65 thermal camera, and BeSensed tactile skins provide dense sensor coverage. Compute is a Jetson Orin AGX for real‑time control and a cluster of 4× NVIDIA H100 GPUs for simulation and LLM inference, linked via 100 Gbps InfiniBand. The enclosure is cleanroom‑compatible with 12 material bays.

The software stack comprises real‑time Xenomai processes, ROS 2 nodes for perception and MPC, a gRPC‑based deliberative layer hosting the CIR runtime and reasoning engine, and a knowledge layer with PINNs, OpenFOAM, FEniCSx, Lean 4, and the governance ledger. OPC UA handles industrial I/O. Resource budgets per tier are tabulated and enforced by the MPC.

