12. Computational Complexity Analysis

Capsule validation: $O(|\mathcal{M}| \cdot P_{\text{Lean}} + N_{\text{val}} \cdot |\mathcal{P}|)$, with $P_{\text{Lean}}$ polynomial in term size.

Knowledge extraction: Dominated by retrieval‑augmented autoformalisation, $O(|\mathcal{D}| \cdot N_{\text{tokens}} \cdot (T_{\text{LLM}} + T_{\text{retrieve}}))$, where retrieval overhead is logarithmic in the proof database size.

Reasoning: MCTS complexity $O(N_{\text{iter}} \cdot B \cdot T_{\text{rollout}})$, with $T_{\text{rollout}}$ at L0 (1 ms). With 1000 iterations and branching 24, this is ~24 s. Lean kernel verification adds $O(|\pi| \cdot N_{\text{saa}} \cdot P_{\text{Lean}})$.

Simulation: L0: 1 ms per evaluation; L1: $O(N_{\text{sim}} \cdot T_{\text{step}})$ parallelised over GPU; L2: $O(N_{\text{mesh}}^{4/3})$.

Execution: Contact‑implicit MPC solves a QP with horizon $H=20$, state dim 14, control dim 14, and up to 10 contacts; complexity $O(H \cdot (n_s + n_u + n_c)^3)$ per control step, ~2 ms on Jetson Orin AGX. CBF filtering adds an extra QP of similar dimension, solvable in microseconds.

World model: VCL update per task uses a diagonal Gaussian, $O(K_{\text{mc}} \cdot d_{\text{param}})$ per gradient step; FO‑MAML outer loop adds a factor of 2 over standard training.

Total pipeline latency per capsule iteration is ~30 s deliberation plus simulation and physical execution, with pipelining enabling concurrent capsule stages.

